"""Curated entries of the pair catalogue: z(A, B) coordinates of the r13 atlas (272 SPIs) and a few pyspi-free
partners, each with its reading under docs/interpreting-spi-pairs.md. Numbers (reliability, z0, null SD, atlas nets)
are attached by build.py from committed JSONs; nothing here is computed.

Field conventions:
  level: estimator | assumption | principled (non-minimal with a known Gaussian relation) | control | diagnostic
  tier: higher-order (Gaussian expectation fixed by second-order structure, so real - IAAFT reads the departure)
        | linear-spectral (fixed by the cross-spectrum: degenerate under spectrum-final IAAFT, needs zero-phase or
        stationary nulls with the state's cross-spectrum) | linear-static (fixed by the zero-lag covariance) | none
  interp: 0-3, how clean the character reading is if the controls hold (3: one assumption apart, or a verified
        Gaussian relation, and the remaining consequences are controllable)
  null_ok: 1 a valid null exists with known construction; .5 a null exists but is imperfect for this statistic;
        0 no usable null
  new: SPIs that are not in the bank (pyspi-free partners); build.py takes reliability from the bank partner only.
"""

LO, HI, BB = 'fmin-0_fmax-0-25', 'fmin-0-25_fmax-0-5', 'fmin-0_fmax-0-5'
